fact WorkItem(id: "WI-671", description: some(value: "scaland: nested query variables are never bound. VarPath models only depth-1 arg paths (Root | Arg(single ArgPos)) and the discrim query-side descends into a nested Term.Fn with bindPaths=false (SubstTree.queryArgValue), so a query var BELOW the top argument level is captured with no binding. E.g. query p(g(?x)) against fact p(g(42)) succeeds with ?x UNBOUND (silent wrong binding); a rule-body goal q(f(?x)) against q(f(5)) likewise. Head-side nested vars (DeBruijn, captured whole as BindValue.TermVal then opened by withFreshVars) are fine — only nested QUERY/goal vars are affected. Pre-existing (untouched by WI-637, which only swapped the Term.Var accessor in those functions); uncovered by the suite; found during WI-637 /code-review. FIX: extend VarPath to a nested path (sequence of ArgPos) + extractAtPath descent, and thread bindPaths through nested Fn descent on the query side (rustland reference: nested VarPath + extract_value_at_path, WI-373 gap 3). ACCEPTANCE: sbt test green + regression test (query p(g(?x)) vs fact p(g(42)) binds ?x=42)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "scaland-sbt-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-10T07:37:50Z"))

